  "Number": 9,
  "Question": "For a sale, a store owner reduces the price of a \\(\\$10\\) scarf by \\(20\\%.\\) Later the price is lowered again, this time by one-half the reduced price. The price is now",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\( \\$2.00 \\)",
    "B": "\\(\\$3.75 \\)",
    "C": "\\(\\$4.00 \\)",
    "D": "\\(\\$4.90 \\)",
    "E": "\\(\\$6.40 \\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "The second reduction is based on the price after the first discount. Since \\(20\\%=0.20\\), the first reduction is \\(0.20\\times10=2\\) dollars, leaving \\(10-2=8\\) dollars.\n\nThe next reduction removes half of \\(8\\) dollars, so the final price is\n\\[\n8-\\frac82=8-4=4\\text{ dollars}.\n\\]\nThe price is \\(\\$4.00\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{C}\\).",
